<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Batlokwa Chiefdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1800 CE – 1853 CE (approx.) · capital Joalaboholo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Sotho-speaking Tlokwa chiefdom led by the regent MaNthatisi and her son Sekonyela, a major power and raider during the wars of the 1820s.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Tlokwa were a Sotho-speaking people of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilge-river">Wilge</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caledon-river">Caledon</a> river region. When <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hlubi-chiefdom">Hlubi</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/swazi-kingdom">Ngwane</a> refugees broke into the highveld in the early 1820s, the regent MaNthatisi led the Tlokwa on a long series of migrations and raids that made her name feared across the interior, before they settled around the mountain fortresses of Joalaboholo and Marabeng near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ficksburg">Ficksburg</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Power rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, mountain strongholds and fighting men drawn from many uprooted groups. MaNthatisi handed authority to her son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sekonyela">Sekonyela</a>, whose rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moshoeshoe-i">Moshoeshoe</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/basotho-kingdom">Basotho Kingdom</a> dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caledon-river">Caledon</a> valley for two decades. Sekonyela received Wesleyan missionaries but kept to traditional religion, and he clashed in turn with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a>: around the end of 1837 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piet-retief">Piet Retief</a> tricked him into handing over cattle taken from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingane">Dingane</a>, along with his horses and guns.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1853 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moshoeshoe-i">Moshoeshoe</a> stormed the Tlokwa strongholds and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sekonyela">Sekonyela</a> fled; he died in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/orange-free-state">Orange Free State</a>. Most of his people were absorbed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sotho-people">Basotho</a>, while others later settled at Witsieshoek in the Free State, where a Tlokwa chieftaincy survives.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1800 CE – 1853 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.52%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1800 CE – 1853 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Joalaboholo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>MaNthatisi, Sekonyela</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sotho traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sesotho</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a>, <a href="/countries/lesotho">Lesotho</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tlokwa, Mantatisi's Tlokwa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1826&amp;focus=batlokwa-chiefdom" aria-label="Batlokwa Chiefdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5292 3267 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Batlokwa Chiefdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5721 3507h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5612 3523h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5612 3523h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day South Africa. <a href="/atlas?year=1826&amp;focus=batlokwa-chiefdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

